{"Title":"An Act relative to municipal parking","BillNumber":"H412","DocketNumber":"HD1867","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"djh1","Name":"Daniel J. Hunt","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/djh1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T18:57:06.56"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"djh1","Name":"Daniel J. Hunt","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/djh1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T18:57:06.56"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H412/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Hunt of Boston, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 412) of Daniel J. Hunt that the Executive Office of Housing and Economic Development and the Department of Revenue be directed to issue a report relative to the ways agencies of the Commonwealth can expand the availability of business district parking within urban areas.  Economic Development and Emerging Technologies.","DocumentText":"\tThe Secretary of Executive office of Housing and Economic Development, in consultation with the Commissioner of the Department of Revenue, shall issue a report relative to the ways state government agencies can expand the availability of business district parking within urban areas and file that report with the Clerks of the House and Senate on or before November 30, 2024. This report may review tax incentives, grants, and a special tax status for private lot owners with some level of public use or benefit.     \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J12","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J12"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}